window.GLOSS={};
window.EN={"1":"Having liberated the northern peninsula, Celice and his companions made Miloah Castle their forward base,","2":"and set about charting the path they should take from here on.","3":"Beyond Miloah Castle lay a chain of harsh mountains, the land of the dragon knights: Thracia.","4":"King Travant of Thracia had allied himself with Emperor Arvis,","5":"ruling this remote region as the sole ally of the Grannvale Empire.","6":"In the Thracian capital he stationed his two children, Prince Arion and Princess Altena;","7":"at Capathogia Castle, the renowned general known as the Shield of Thracia, Hannibal;","8":"at Lutecia Castle, the king's trusted aide, General Dislar;","9":"and at Grutia Castle, Bishop Judah of the dark cult, dispatched from the Empire —","10":"and with them, he prepared for all-out confrontation with the Liberation Army.","11":"The people of Thracia feared Celice and his companions as invaders,","12":"and were ready to take up arms themselves to fight them.","13":"Was there any justice in this fight? For whose sake were they fighting?","14":"For Celice and his companions, this was their first true trial...","15":"(Travant): Altena! What is the meaning of this! Why didn't you attack Manster!?","16":"(Altena): Father... but...","17":"(Travant): I don't want to hear excuses! Altena, don't you dare take me for a fool.","18":"(Travant): Even though you're a woman, you excel at the art of war, and I expected you, together with Arion, to serve as my hands and feet.","19":"(Travant): And yet, look at this — you ignored my orders, lost your men for nothing, and came crawling back here,","20":"(Travant): I'm... utterly disappointed in you.","21":"(Altena): I'm sorry, but, father! Is it really happiness for the people of Thracia","22":"(Altena): to grow rich by oppressing the people of other nations? Father, what you're doing is simply too...","23":"(Arion): Silence, Altena. This isn't something for the likes of you to speak up about. Be quiet and obey father for now!","24":"(Arion): Father, Altena is still young. Facing real battle for the first time, her emotions must simply be running high.","25":"(Arion): Please, just this once, forgive her.","26":"(Travant): Arion, it's because you coddle her like this that Altena gets so full of herself.","27":"(Travant): Altena, I'll give you one more chance. Lead the dragon knight corps and retake Miloah.","28":"(Travant): If you fail again this time, I won't show mercy even to my own daughter. Understood?","29":"(Altena): Yes.........","30":"(Travant): Heh, blood is a frightening thing... that girl hates me...","31":"(Arion): Father, Altena is still a child. Spoiled by you, she just lashes out with whatever resentful words come to mind...","32":"(Travant): Enough of that... I'm going to Capathogia Castle. That Hannibal fellow seems unhappy with my methods.","33":"(Travant): I need to take precautions, in case he betrays us.","34":"(Arion): ...father is afraid... whatever has happened to him...","35":"(Travant): General Hannibal, the rebels have seized Miloah Castle. Altena is already moving to attack.","36":"(Travant): You too, send out your armored knight corps.","37":"(Hannibal): Your Majesty, as I've said many times already, this fight is meaningless.","38":"(Hannibal): We should make peace with the Liberation Army and focus on building up our national strength for now.","39":"(Hannibal): Joining hands with the Empire is out of the question — it would turn the people against us.","40":"(Travant): Don't talk nonsense! They killed my men and stole Miloah Castle!","41":"(Travant): There's no making peace now!","42":"(Hannibal): I see... there's no helping it, then.","43":"(Travant): You're not planning to betray me, are you, Hannibal?","44":"(Hannibal): I am a warrior of some renown myself. There's no way I would ever betray you!","45":"(Travant): Is that so. Then, let me see proof of that loyalty.","46":"(Travant): Until this battle is over, I'll be keeping your son with me.","47":"(Hannibal): King Travant! Do you not trust me at all!?","48":"(Travant): If you have no intention of betraying me, then you have no reason to worry about your son's life.","49":"(Hannibal): What in the world...","50":"(Travant): Bring Hannibal's son here!","51":"(Coirpre): Father...","52":"(Hannibal): Coirpre... I'm sorry...","53":"(Travant): Don't worry. Once this battle is over, I'll give him back.","54":"(Travant): But Hannibal, he isn't even your real child, is he — and yet you dote on him this much?","55":"(Hannibal): Coirpre is my treasure. Blood ties have nothing to do with it...","56":"(Travant): Hahaha, so even Thracia's great general has a weakness for children. Well then, I'm counting on you, Hannibal!","57":"(Travant): Dislar, the battle is about to begin. Is the castle's defense without fault?","58":"(Dislar): Why, Your Majesty Travant, welcome. What an honor to have you visit.","59":"(Dislar): Lutecia Castle's defenses are perfect — please, rest assured.","60":"(Travant): I'm counting on you. That Hannibal of Capathogia can't be trusted.","61":"(Travant): I've taken his son hostage. Keep watch over him here at Lutecia Castle.","62":"(Dislar): Yes, leave it to me. But, should Hannibal ever try to betray us...","63":"(Travant): At that time, kill the boy. Just because he's a child, show no mercy.","64":"(Dislar): Yes sir, understood.","65":"(Travant): Lord Judah, as per our long-standing pact, Emperor Arvis will be sending reinforcements, won't he?","66":"(Judah): King Travant, you really are a cautious man. Rest assured — the Imperial Knights are already on their way here.","67":"(Travant): I see, then good. I'll leave the defense of this castle in your hands.","68":"(Travant): Watch out, so the rebels don't catch you off guard!","69":"(Levin (Strategist)): It seems the dragon knight corps has set out from Thracia. This is it, Celice — don't let your guard down.","70":"(Celice): But Levin, our enemy is supposed to be the Empire. Is there really any meaning to this fight?","71":"(Levin (Strategist)): Whether there's meaning in it or not depends entirely on how you fight it.","72":"(Levin (Strategist)): This battle can no longer be avoided. There's no turning back now.","73":"(Celice): But that dragon knight who watched us from the mountains of Manster... she looked so terribly sad.","74":"(Celice): To think we might have to fight someone like that...","75":"(Levin (Strategist)): Celice! Enough of that!! This is war.","76":"(Levin (Strategist)): If you've grown sick of fighting, then go back to Tirnanog!","77":"(Celice): Levin.........","78":"(Hannibal): Hmm... it seems the rebels have begun their advance.","79":"(Kanatz): Lord Hannibal, please give the order to attack.","80":"(Hannibal): No, wait. We'll focus solely on defending the castle. We must avoid any needless fighting.","81":"(Kanatz): But, in that case...","82":"(Hannibal): I know about my son's situation... .........but, in any case, let's watch how things go for now.","83":"(Hannibal): Kanatz, sorry, but I need you to guard the castle.","84":"(Kanatz): Yes sir, as you command!","85":"(Altena): From here, I will retake Miloah Castle. All troops, attack the rebels!","86":"(Dislar): Who'd have thought, at my age, I'd end up babysitting some brat...","87":"(Coirpre): Mister Dislar, please let me go. My father doesn't want to fight.","88":"(Coirpre): I don't want him to force himself to fight for my sake!","89":"(Dislar): Quiet! Be silent!!","90":"(Dislar): That man was once called the Shield of Thracia — for him to try to run away now would be laughable. He'll fight alongside us to the very end!","91":"(Coirpre): Father... I'm sorry.","92":"(Fabal): Hey, Patty! Are you still stealing things!?","93":"(Patty): Yeah, now and then, just a little.","94":"(Fabal): Enough already. No matter how much you say it's from the enemy, I don't like it.","95":"(Patty): It's not like I do it because I want to, you know.","96":"(Patty): But when I think of the Liberation Army's finances, there's no helping it!","97":"(Fabal): But still... there are people out there who find it amusing, saying things like \"a pirate's child really is a thief after all.\"","98":"(Fabal): Of course, I punched them out, but...","99":"(Patty): Let those who want to talk, talk — I don't care.","100":"(Patty): Because our mother was a warrior descended from the blood of the holy warrior Ulir, you know.","101":"(Patty): When I heard that story from Levin, I was so happy I cried.","102":"(Fabal): Yeah, me too... I mean, we were orphans, and we'd lived such a miserable life all this time.","103":"(Fabal): I never imagined mother was someone so noble. Patty, do you remember anything about mother?","104":"(Patty): No, nothing at all... what about you, brother?","105":"(Fabal): I... just a little... she was so beautiful... and such a kind person...","106":"(Patty): So mother... did Mother Brigid die?","107":"(Fabal): I don't know that. Patty, once this war is over, let's go search for her together.","108":"(Fabal): Mother Brigid... and... our father too, whose name we still don't even know...","109":"(Asaello): Hey, Daisy! Are you still stealing things!?","110":"(Daisy): Yeah, now and then, just a little.","111":"(Asaello): Enough already. No matter how much you say it's from the enemy, I don't like it.","112":"(Daisy): It's not like I do it because I want to, you know.","113":"(Daisy): But when I think about the Liberation Army's finances, there's no helping it!","114":"(Asaello): But still...","115":"(Daisy): And besides, I have to send money to the children I left behind in Conote too — it's hard for me too, you know.","116":"(Asaello): Yeah, that's true... I wonder if they're doing alright.","117":"(Daisy): Asaello, you'd better pitch in too. Even if you win prize money at the arena, don't go wasting it!","118":"(Asaello): Ugh, I think that backfired on me...","119":"(Leaf): Please wait! Sister!!","120":"(Altena): Sister, you say!? ...who are you! Why are you calling me your sister!","121":"(Leaf): I'm... Leaf of Leonster.","122":"(Altena): Leaf? I see, so you're the prince of Leonster.","123":"(Altena): I am Travant's daughter, Altena. Please don't say such sleepy nonsense.","124":"(Leaf): You are the child of my own parents, Quan and Ethlyn. Seventeen years ago, the two of them were killed by Travant.","125":"(Leaf): My sister, who was still young at the time, went missing, along with Leonster's treasure, the Gaebolg.","126":"(Leaf): That lance you're holding right now — that is Leonster's Gaebolg.","127":"(Altena): What did you say!?","128":"(Altena): Then, the man I believed to be my father was actually my real father's enemy... surely not... that can't be...","129":"(Leaf): Please, look at me. Whether what I've said is a lie or not — you should be able to tell just by looking.","130":"(Leaf): Sister, please...","131":"(Altena): Ngh... why!? Why can't I say your words are a lie!!","132":"(Leaf): Sister...!!","133":"(Altena): Wait! ...I'm going to go confirm this with father. Everything starts from there!!","134":"(Travant): Altena, what on earth do you think you're doing — abandoning your men again and fleeing back here alone!","135":"(Altena): Father! There's something I need to ask you. Is it true that I'm not really your daughter!?","136":"(Altena): Am I King Quan's daughter!","137":"(Travant): Heh... so you've finally learned the truth. Well, fine — I always knew a day like this would come.","138":"(Travant): You are indeed Quan's daughter. But so what?","139":"(Travant): It was I who raised you. That fact doesn't change, does it.","140":"(Altena): ...then, my real parents — father, you...","141":"(Travant): Hehehe, that's right. Your real parents, Quan and Ethlyn, I killed them myself. But what of it?","142":"(Travant): In war, one kills and is killed. There's no point in bringing that up now.","143":"(Altena): Ngh... I can't forgive this, deceiving me like this... Father! ...no, Travant!!","144":"(Arion): Stop it! Altena!","145":"(Altena): Brother! Don't try to stop me! I will kill this man. I won't let anyone get in my way!","146":"(Arion): I won't allow that! If you're going to raise your blade against father, then I will be the one to face you!","147":"(Altena): W-, wait! I can't fight you, brother!!","148":"(Arion): It's too late for that now... die, Altena!","149":"(Altena): A-, brother.........","150":"(Travant): ...Arion. Did you kill Altena? You didn't need to go that far...","151":"(Travant): Well, never mind. Arion, with things as they are, I'll have to step in myself. There's no other way left now.","152":"(Travant): I entrust the castle's defense to you.","153":"(Arion): Leave it to me, father.","154":"(Travant): I'll leave this lance in your care. Understand, you must protect Thracia.","155":"(Arion): Father, isn't this the lance Gungnir?","156":"(Arion): Just as you're about to go into battle yourself, why would you hand this to me? Could it be... father?","157":"(Travant): That's enough, I'm tired. From here, do as you see fit. They surely don't hate you as they hate me.","158":"(Arion): Are you telling me to make peace with them? I can't agree to that!","159":"(Travant): That's why I said do as you see fit. Only, don't make the people suffer any more than this. That's my only wish.","160":"(Travant): Well then, farewell, Arion!","161":"(Arion): Father...","162":"(Altena): Stop! The likes of you cannot defeat me!","163":"(Altena): Brother... brother Arion.........","164":"(Arion): Father... Altena... ...has fallen in battle.","165":"(Travant): I see... well, never mind. Arion, with things as they are, I'll have to step in myself.","166":"(Travant): There's no other way left now. I entrust the castle's defense to you.","167":"(Arion): Leave it to me, father.","168":"(Travant): I'll leave this lance in your care. Understand, you must protect Thracia.","169":"(Arion): Father, isn't this the lance Gungnir?","170":"(Arion): Just as you're about to go into battle yourself, why would you hand this to me? Could it be... father?","171":"(Travant): That's enough, I'm tired. From here, do as you see fit. They surely don't hate you as they hate me.","172":"(Arion): Are you telling me to make peace with them? I can't agree to that!","173":"(Travant): That's why I said do as you see fit. Only, don't make the people suffer any more than this. That's my only wish.","174":"(Travant): Well then, farewell, Arion!","175":"(Arion): Father...","176":"(Travant): Hahaha, you rebel small fry, I am Travant.","177":"(Travant): As a parting gift for the afterlife, remember that well!","178":"(Travant): Thracia... my beloved land... guh...","179":"(Altena): Lord Celice, I am Altena, daughter of Quan of Leonster.","180":"(Altena): Having learned the truth from my younger brother, Prince Leaf, I can no longer fight against you. Please, let me join the Liberation Army too.","181":"(Celice): Princess Altena!? Ah, so you're Prince Leaf's elder sister!","182":"(Celice): I heard the story from him, and I've been waiting. Thank you — I'm sure the prince will be overjoyed too.","183":"(Celice): Thank you for making such a brave decision.","184":"(Altena): ...I still can hardly believe it myself. But the moment I looked into Prince Leaf's eyes, I understood everything.","185":"(Altena): Those were the same gentle eyes as my father's...","186":"(Altena): And memories of being a little girl, held in my mother's arms, came flooding back to me, clear as day.","187":"(Celice): But what in the world was King Travant thinking?","188":"(Celice): To kill your parents, and yet still bring you, so young at the time, back to his own country...","189":"(Altena): I heard that my brother wanted to use the lance Gaebolg for himself.","190":"(Altena): And that's why he took me...","191":"(Celice): You mean, he only used you?","192":"(Altena): That... I don't even know myself. Travant is a frightening man, but I believed he was my father...","193":"(Celice): King Travant... he's a hard man to understand.","194":"(Altena): Lord Celice, I have a request. Arion — please, spare at least Prince Arion's life.","195":"(Celice): Yes, I've heard he's an admirable man. I don't want to fight him either. But will he listen to us?","196":"(Altena): Let me try to persuade him once more. So please, just give me a little more time!","197":"(Coirpre): Father, it's me, Coirpre. Please, stop fighting now!","198":"(Coirpre): The Liberation Army has already taken Lutecia Castle!","199":"(Hannibal): Coirpre!? You... you're safe!","200":"(Coirpre): Yeah, father. I want to join Lord Celice's Liberation Army.","201":"(Coirpre): Thracia isn't the Thracia of old anymore. I want to fight for everyone!","202":"(Hannibal): I see... so you've grown up too. Understood, Coirpre. I'll fight alongside Lord Celice as well.","203":"(Coirpre): Yeah, father! Let's liberate Thracia and stand up against the Empire together, everyone!","204":"(Celice): General Hannibal. We ended up fighting a pointless battle. My deepest apologies.","205":"(Hannibal): Lord Celice... I hear you saved my son. It is I who should be apologizing...","206":"(Celice): General, you are an honored warrior, known as the Shield of Thracia.","207":"(Celice): To force you into battle by taking a hostage... King Travant's methods are far too dishonorable.","208":"(Hannibal): That man is pitiable too. Having betrayed others again and again, he's become unable to trust anyone.","209":"(Hannibal): But doing things that way, people's hearts will never follow him...","210":"(Celice): General, please, guide us young ones. We need your strength.","211":"(Hannibal): Hmm, if an old man like me can be of use, I'll lend my strength. Lord Celice, I'm counting on you.","212":"(Lene): You must be Coirpre.","213":"(Coirpre): Ah, y-, yeah...","214":"(Lene): I hear you're an orphan too, Coirpre. Don't you have any memories from when you were small?","215":"(Coirpre): No, none at all. When father found me in the streets of Darna, I was still just a baby, or so I'm told...","216":"(Lene): You too, in Darna!?","217":"(Coirpre): Miss Lene, do you know Darna?","218":"(Lene): I grew up in a convent in that very town.","219":"(Lene): When I was about two years old, I'm told a young woman, who looked like a dancer, left me at the convent.","220":"(Lene): The reason I became a dancer is","221":"(Lene): because I thought that someday, I might be able to meet my mother again.","222":"(Lene): So, embarrassing as it is, I taught myself the dance.","223":"(Coirpre): Huh, Miss Lene, you're really something. I think I misjudged you a little.","224":"(Lene): So you don't like dancers, Coirpre?","225":"(Coirpre): Yeah, I used to hate them. But I like you, Miss Lene.","226":"(Lene): Heh, thank you, Coirpre.","227":"(Laylea): I hear your name is Charlot, is that right?","228":"(Charlot): Eh... and you, miss?","229":"(Laylea): I'm Laylea. Charlot, have you never seen a dancer before?","230":"(Charlot): Um... not yet...","231":"(Laylea): Heheh, come visit again sometime, when you're free — I'll show you my dance.","232":"(Charlot): U-, um, okay...","233":"(Patty): Hmm, so you're Coirpre?","234":"(Patty): I heard you were General Hannibal's child and wondered what kind of impressive person you'd be, but — huh, you're just an ordinary kid.","235":"(Coirpre): You're a kid yourself, aren't you.","236":"(Patty): Well, how rude. Are you saying I look like a child to you?","237":"(Coirpre): Yeah, you do.","238":"(Patty): Hmph... you... you're not cute at all!","239":"(Hannibal): So, it seems I must fight after all... this too, is for Thracia's sake... there's no helping it...","240":"(Hannibal): My son... please, live on...","241":"(Kanatz): This castle was entrusted to me by Lord Hannibal.","242":"(Kanatz): Even at the cost of my life, I will not yield it!","243":"(Kanatz): Lord Hannibal... please, forgive me.","244":"(Dislar): What... the rebels!? Damn it, I let my guard down!","245":"(Dislar): Lord Travant......... ...forgive me...","246":"(Levin (Strategist)): Celice, it seems General Hannibal had his son taken hostage, and was forced to fight us against his will.","247":"(Celice): So that's how it was... I've made a mistake that can never be undone... please forgive me, General Hannibal.","248":"— (only if Hannibal is still alive)","249":"(Levin (Strategist)): Celice, it seems there was a child held captive in the dungeon.","250":"(Celice): Who are you? ...what on earth happened to you?","251":"(Coirpre): I'm Coirpre, General Hannibal's son. And you are...?","252":"(Coirpre): Ah, you're Lord Celice of the Liberation Army!?","253":"(Celice): Yeah, that's right. So you're General Hannibal's son — but why were you locked in a dungeon like this?","254":"(Coirpre): King Travant took me hostage.","255":"(Coirpre): My father didn't want to fight Lord Celice, but he was forced to, for my sake...","256":"(Coirpre): Lord Celice, please! Take me to my father.","257":"(Coirpre): If he knows I'm safe, father should stop fighting. Please, save my father!!","258":"(Celice): So that's how it was...","259":"(Celice): Understood. Let's hurry to General Hannibal at once. There should still be time!","260":"— (only if Hannibal has died)","261":"(Levin (Strategist)): Celice, it seems General Hannibal's son was held captive in this castle as a hostage.","262":"(Celice): Then Hannibal was forced to fight, against his will, for the sake of his child! What a terrible thing...","263":"(Levin (Strategist)): I hear that same Coirpre vanished upon hearing of his father's death.","264":"(Levin (Strategist)): He must hate us now... how tragic.","265":"(Celice): Ngh...","266":"(Judah): Capathogia has fallen into enemy hands!? Hmph, are the people of Thracia nothing but cowards?","267":"(Judah): There's no helping it — strengthen the castle's defenses! We'll hold this castle to the death, until reinforcements arrive from the homeland!","268":"(Musar): So this is Thracia... heh, what an awful wasteland.","269":"(Musar): Well, no matter. We can't let the rebels run wild any longer. All troops, charge!","270":"(Musar): Whoever takes the enemy's head will receive a reward from the Emperor himself. Don't waste this chance!","271":"(Musar): Die, you rebels! Those who defy the Empire deserve nothing but death!","272":"(Musar): Long live the Grannvale Empire...!","273":"(Judah): Damn you... what is this \"Liberation Army\" nonsense... this world has no need for light.","274":"(Judah): The darkness of Lord Loptous shall rule over all!","275":"(Judah): Fuhaha... once Lord Loptous is resurrected... ...the likes of you...","276":"(Celice): Levin, does Arion still intend to keep fighting?","277":"(Levin (Strategist)): We've sent envoys to propose a truce many times, but he won't listen.","278":"(Levin (Strategist)): For the pride of the dragon knights, he says he'll fight to the very end.","279":"(Levin (Strategist)): Arion of Thracia... I thought he was a somewhat wiser man than this...","280":"(Levin (Strategist)): Celice, there's no helping it now. All that's left is the final battle.","281":"(Celice): Ngh... why... why must it come to this...","282":"(Julia): Lord Celice, are you injured anywhere?","283":"(Celice): No, I'm fine. You be careful too, Julia.","284":"(Julia): Lord Celice...","285":"(Celice): Hm? What's wrong?","286":"(Julia): No, it's nothing.........","287":"(Celice): You're acting a little strange today, Julia. Is there something on your mind?","288":"(Julia): ...somehow, I feel uneasy... I feel as though, if I'm ever separated from you, Lord Celice, we'll never be able to meet again.","289":"(Julia): I'm... scared...","290":"(Celice): It's alright, Julia.","291":"(Celice): I told you before, didn't I — I decided I would protect you. So please, trust me.","292":"(Julia): Yes... I do trust you... I'm sorry, Lord Celice... I keep troubling you like this.","293":"(Celice): It's a long journey — the exhaustion is catching up with you.","294":"(Celice): Once this battle is over, we'll go to the free city of Miletos, so you can rest there for a while.","295":"(Celice): Oh, that's right — why don't the two of us go shopping in town? I'll buy you whatever you like.","296":"(Celice): But nothing too expensive, alright — Levin would scold me for it.","297":"(Julia): Oh, Lord Celice... but, I'm happy... thank you...","298":"(Celice): You finally smiled — I'm glad.","299":"(Julia): Lord Celice, please close your eyes for just a moment...","300":"(Celice): Hm? ...what's wrong...?","301":"(Julia): I'm going to cast the Magic Shield spell on you, to raise your magic defense.","302":"(Celice): Eh!? But if you use that spell, won't it put you in danger?","303":"(Julia): It's alright... please, think of it as my last little selfishness, and just do as I ask.","304":"(Celice): Julia...","305":"(Julia): May the gods' protection be upon you, Lord Celice...","306":"(Finn): Lady Altena, I am Finn, a knight of Leonster. Please, allow me to introduce myself.","307":"(Altena): So you're Sir Finn. I've heard about you from Leaf.","308":"(Altena): Thank you for protecting my brother all this time. Let me offer you my thanks.","309":"(Finn): No, Lady Altena... it is I who must apologize to you.","310":"(Finn): Never imagining you were still alive, I lived right next door in a neighboring country, and yet could not save you.","311":"(Finn): Now, all I can do is regret it deeply.........","312":"(Altena): Sir Finn... are you... crying...? Why...","313":"(Finn): This is... I've shown you an unbecoming sight. I'm very sorry.........","314":"(Altena): I have a faint memory... Finn... I loved you so much... I always used to cling to you...","315":"(Altena): That's right, isn't it, Sir Finn...","316":"(Finn): Lady Altena, I...","317":"(Hannibal): Why, Lady Altena, I've heard your story. You too have had a hard time of it.","318":"(Altena): General Hannibal... so you're cooperating with the Liberation Army too?","319":"(Altena): I'm so glad... if even you had become an enemy, I don't think I could have fought.","320":"(Hannibal): Mm, and so, what of Lord Arion? What has become of him?","321":"(Altena): My brother... no, Arion, won't listen to a word I say. If possible, I'd like you to be the one to persuade him, General.","322":"(Hannibal): If even the princess's words won't work, there's no other way left.","323":"(Hannibal): Lord Arion wishes to die as a warrior, I imagine. It's best to give up on changing his mind.","324":"(Altena): But, General Hannibal!","325":"(Hannibal): I understand how you feel... but that's just the way men are.","326":"(Hannibal): Lord Arion doesn't want to show you an unbecoming sight, Princess — you must understand that, Princess Altena...","327":"(Hannibal): Charlot.........","328":"(Charlot): Eh? Ah, father, what's wrong?","329":"(Hannibal): I'm sorry about the other day, putting you through such an awful ordeal for my sake...","330":"(Hannibal): Perhaps it would have been better for you to be raised in an ordinary household, rather than by a soldier like me...","331":"(Charlot): Father! That's not true at all! I feel so fulfilled right now.","332":"(Charlot): Because I can put my strength to use for the sake of peace. There's nothing that makes me happier than that.","333":"(Hannibal): I see...","334":"(Charlot): And you know,","335":"(Hannibal): ...hm?","336":"(Charlot): I'm proud of you, father.","337":"(Charlot): The people of Capathogia adore you, and besides, you raised me, an orphan, as your own.","338":"(Hannibal): I see... thank you... you've grown into a fine person...","339":"(Hannibal): That reminds me, I meant to give you this staff. It had been sleeping deep within the castle, but you should be able to use it.","340":"(Charlot): Wow, this looks like an amazing staff. Thank you, father.","341":"(Arion): So you've come... alright, let's go! Victory, or death... that depends entirely on how you fight!","342":"(Arion): All troops, charge the enemy!!","343":"(Arion): Heh... how foolish... can you not see this heavenly lance Gungnir before your very eyes...","344":"(Arion): Wh-, what... how could this be... ngh, how regrettable... Altena...","345":"(Julius): Arion, I cannot let you die just yet... come to me... hahahaha...","346":"(Celice): Levin, is it true that Arion has vanished?","347":"(Levin (Strategist)): Yes. Someone saw Prince Julius — it seems he rescued him and carried him away.","348":"(Celice): Prince Julius? Emperor Arvis's son?","349":"(Levin (Strategist)): Mm, and he's your half-brother, on your mother's side.","350":"(Celice): The same mother as me...","351":"(Levin (Strategist)): That's right... Princess Deirdre. Prince Julius inherited his power as a shaman from his mother.","352":"(Levin (Strategist)): That's why Return and Recover come to him as naturally as breathing.","353":"(Levin (Strategist)): But that's not all... Prince Julius's true power is...","354":"(Celice): Eh...?","355":"(Levin (Strategist)): ...the dark god, Loptous...","356":"(Elder): Is it true that a priest of the dark cult has come to Grutia?","357":"(Elder): I understand King Travant's feelings, but still,","358":"(Elder): joining hands with the Loptr cult is something he absolutely must never do... ahh, the king has made a grave mistake!","359":"(Elder): I'll give you this Barrier Ring. Please, I beg you, save Thracia!","360":"(Villager (man)): General Dislar of Lutecia is nothing but Travant's lapdog.","361":"(Villager (man)): He throws his weight around despite having no real power — he's a truly unpleasant fellow!","362":"— (only before Musar is defeated)","363":"(Villager (man)): I heard a rumor that reinforcements are coming from the Empire.","364":"(Villager (man)): The commander is a Silesian knight named Musar — I hear the rebels killed his father.","365":"(Villager (man)): He seems to hate you all, so be careful.","366":"— (after Musar is defeated)","367":"(Villager (man)): Wow, you all are really something — did you really defeat those reinforcements that came from the Empire?","368":"(Auntie): General Hannibal of Capathogia is one of the one or two greatest generals in all of Thracia.","369":"(Auntie): He's been charging across battlefields since he was young, so he never married, but a dozen or so years ago, he took in an orphan,","370":"(Auntie): and raised him like his own child ever since. He's truly such a kind man.","371":"(Old woman): King Travant is a cold-hearted man, but Prince Arion and Princess Altena are both such kind children.","372":"(Old woman): The two of them have been close ever since they were small — I just hope nothing terrible happens to them...","373":"(Villager (man)): The villages around here used to belong peacefully to the Leonster royal family, as their territory.","374":"(Villager (man)): But after the last war, we ended up occupied by the Thracian army.","375":"(Villager (man)): Heh heh heh ♥","376":"(Hawk): .........?","377":"(Villager (man)): The other day, I got confessed to by a girl, under the tree in the square, you see...","378":"(Villager (man)): I'd like to share this happy feeling with you too.","379":"(Hawk): ..........","380":"(Villager (man)): That's right! You're with the Liberation Army, aren't you — here, take this secret scroll and medicine passed down in our village!","381":"(Hawk): T-, thanks...","382":"(Villager (man)): Love is a wonderful thing, isn't it... you should fall in love too."};
